            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "compiled geometry and plant characterization",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.characterize_arm"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial unresolved distinction is whether the official target set contains static branch or Jacobian/limit obstructions, versus failures being caused by sampled-data dynamics and hold stabilization. Exhaustive branch-wise IK with compiled-model forward residuals will resolve the geometric side; compiled masses, actuator transmission, torque-response probes, and free decay will constrain the dynamic interpretation. A finding of infeasible targets or near-singular feasible branches would redirect the campaign toward posture/geometry handling. If targets are feasible with margin and actuation is credible, the next direction should measure or train closed-loop reach-and-hold behavior and diagnose first-entry velocity and interruptions."
      },
